{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "F32AnEnumMemberCannotBeZero",
    "description": "Finding F32. An `enums` member must be a POSITIVE integer -- `esm-schema.json`'s `EnumDeclaration.additionalProperties` is `{\"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1}` -- so an identifier whose value is 0 cannot be named. MOVES has several, and one of them is load-bearing.\n\n`operatingmode.opModeID = 0` is Braking. It is not a sentinel, not a default and not an absence: it is the operating mode a decelerating second is classified into, it carries its own emission rate, and in `mixed-onroad` it is 2.0% of the weekend and 5.6% of the weekday operating-mode distribution. `regulatoryclass.regClassID = 0` (\"Doesn't Matter\"), `modelyeargroup.modelYearGroupID = 0` and `fuelusagefraction.modelYearGroupID = 0` (a wildcard) are three more, in three other tables.\n\nWHAT IT COSTS. The convention this repository follows is that an identifier VALUE is written once, in an `enums` block, and referenced by name everywhere else (docs/esm-conventions.md §4). A zero-valued identifier has to be written as a bare `0.0` literal with a comment instead, and the comment is the only thing connecting it to the table it came from. In `fixtures/mixed-onroad.esm` that is `run_brakingOpModeID`, which three equations key on. A reader who renumbers operating modes has to find a literal rather than an enum member.\n\nWHY THE RULE PROBABLY EXISTS, and why it does not hold. `minimum: 1` reads like a guard against an enum member being confused with an absent one, which is a real hazard for a 1-based index set. But an `enums` member is not an index: `enum` resolves to a NUMBER used in arithmetic and in `join.on` key comparisons, and 0 is an ordinary value there. The two 1-based things in the format -- index-set coordinates and `makearray` regions -- are separate constructs with their own validation.\n\nFIX SHAPE. Drop the `minimum` from `EnumDeclaration.additionalProperties`, or lower it to allow the whole integer range. Negative values matter too and for the same reason: `opmodepolprocassoc.polProcessID = -1` marks the unassociated drive-cycle modes (24 of its 27 rows in the `process-evap-leaks` snapshot), and `driveschedule` speeds aside, a MOVES table that uses -1 as a real code is not unusual.\n\nThis repro is expected to FAIL: it does not validate. `./run-tests.sh` reads a repro that starts passing as an upstream fix and says so.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": ["finding", "enums", "identifiers"]
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "row_ax": { "kind": "interval", "size": 2 }
  },
  "enums": {
    "operating_mode": { "Braking": 0, "Idling": 1 }
  },
  "models": {
    "F32AnEnumMemberCannotBeZero": {
      "variables": {
        "modeID": {
          "type": "unknown", "units": "1", "shape": ["row_ax"],
          "description": "The two operating modes MOVES's drive-cycle classification assigns outside the VSP bins, named rather than written as literals. Braking is 0 and Idling is 1, and only one of the two can be an enum member today."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "modeID",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "makearray", "args": [],
            "regions": [[[1, 1]], [[2, 2]]],
            "values": [
              { "op": "enum", "args": ["operating_mode", "Braking"] },
              { "op": "enum", "args": ["operating_mode", "Idling"] }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "a_zero_valued_identifier_can_be_named",
          "description": "The intended behaviour, which is what makes this repro fail today: the document does not validate, with `/enums/operating_mode/Braking: 0 is less than the minimum of 1`. When it starts passing, fixtures/mixed-onroad.esm's `run_brakingOpModeID` literal and the three equations that key on it can go back to naming the mode.",
          "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 0.0 },
          "assertions": [
            { "variable": "modeID", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0, "coords": { "row_ax": 1 } },
            { "variable": "modeID", "time": 0.0, "expected": 1.0, "coords": { "row_ax": 2 } }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
